    "question": "Thomas, Toby, and Rebecca worked a total of 157 hours in one week.  Thomas worked x hours.  Toby worked 10 hours less than twice what Thomas worked, and Rebecca worked 8 hours less than Toby.  How many hours did Rebecca work?",
    "gold": "56",
    "answer": "Toby: 2x-10\nRebecca: (2x-10)-8=2x-18\nTotal:2x-10+2x-18+x=157\n5x-28=157\n5x=185\nx=<<37=37>>37 hours\nRebecca:2(37)-18=56 hours\n#### 56"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many hours Rebecca worked, we need to set up and solve a system of equations based on the information given.\n\nLet's define the variables:\n- Let \\( T \\) be the number of hours Thomas worked.\n- Let \\( B \\) be the number of hours Rebecca worked.\n\nFrom the problem, we know the following:\n1. The total number of hours worked by Thomas, Toby, and Rebecca is 157.\n2. Toby worked 10 hours less than twice what Thomas worked.\n3. Rebecca worked 8 hours less than Toby.\n\nWe can express these relationships with the following equations:\n1. \\( T + B + (2T - 10) = 157 \\)\n2. \\( B = (2T - 10) - 8 \\)\n\nFirst, simplify the first equation:\n\\[ T + B + 2T - 10 = 157 \\]\n\\[ 3T + B - 10 = 157 \\]\n\\[ 3T + B = 167 \\]\n\nNext, simplify the second equation:\n\\[ B = 2T - 10 - 8 \\]\n\\[ B = 2T - 18 \\]\n\nNow we have a system of two equations:\n1. \\( 3T + B = 167 \\)\n2. \\( B = 2T - 18 \\)\n\nWe can substitute the expression for \\( B \\) from the second equation into the first equation:\n\\[ 3T + (2T - 18) = 167 \\]\n\\[ 3T + 2T - 18 = 167 \\]\n\\[ 5T - 18 = 167 \\]\n\\[ 5T = 185 \\]\n\\[ T = 37 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( T = 37 \\), we can substitute this value back into the second equation to find \\( B \\):\n\\[ B = 2(37) - 18 \\]\n\\[ B = 74 - 18 \\]\n\\[ B = 56 \\]\n\nTherefore, Rebecca worked \\(\\boxed{56}\\) hours.",
